  "observations": [
    "The candidate learns the sampled exposed TRAIN prefixes: 11/12 complete against 0/12, with five of six contrasted pairs correct on both branches. The remaining negation pair repeats sendero rojo in both branches.",
    "Exact development matching is 0/12, but semantic reading finds one acceptable uncertainty paraphrase and one partial corrected schedule. There is therefore limited observed transfer, below the fixed criterion.",
    "The two actual-history development dialogues remain wholly incorrect; successful ideal TRAIN prefixes do not demonstrate free conversational competence.",
    "No declared whole TRAIN names or full values occur literally in the candidate development outputs. It is inaccurate to describe these responses as observed copies of TRAIN names/values.",
    "Several wrong development answers select values supplied for another development person: Caelun’s Thursday schedule for Zumira, Ulmera’s bottle for Dovian, and Osvira’s sheet for Leimar. This suggests binding and wording transfer problems beyond simple unknown-token coverage.",
    "Shorter outputs and zero token-budget stops improve technical behavior but do not resolve semantic failures. Malformed names and missing required values persist."
  ],
  "hypothesisStatus": "Training/memorization control learns; proposed broad generalization criterion fails. No model promotion. The one semantic transfer case has explicit reviewer uncertainty.",
  "nextMinimalDiagnostic": {
    "purpose": "Separate unseen lexical binding from unseen request wording and reliance on ideal history before changing architecture or repeating broad training.",
    "design": "Freeze new development-only factorial cases for the same fixed parent/candidate: (A) TRAIN wording and names with new values; (B) TRAIN wording/values with new names; (C) new wording with TRAIN names/values; (D) reverse mention order while preserving facts and requests. Keep related variants together, preserve these exposed cases as development, and compare raw generation plus context-swap likelihood. Do not use the reserved final.",
    "interpretation": "A/B failure isolates lexical/value binding; C-only failure isolates linguistic formulation; mention-order failure exposes a positional shortcut. Successful teacher-forced prefixes but failed generated history identify recovery/continuity failure. These are hypotheses until the new control is executed.",
